PART 9 — QUICK REFERENCE: SHELL ALIASES
================================================================================

Add these to ~/.bashrc for convenience:

    # === TELLO (drone_a, 192.168.10.x, CycloneDDS) ===
    alias ros-drone-a='
    export RMW_IMPLEMENTATION=rmw_cyclonedds_cpp &&
    export ROS_DOMAIN_ID=10
    '

    # === ASTRO (drone_b, 192.168.8.x, Zenoh) ===
    alias ros-drone-b='
    export RMW_IMPLEMENTATION=rmw_zenoh_cpp &&
    export ASTRO_NUM=4 &&
    export ROS_DOMAIN_ID=$ASTRO_NUM &&
    export ZENOH_CONFIG_OVERRIDE="mode=\"client\";connect/endpoints=[\"tcp/192.168.8.2${ASTRO_NUM}:7447\"]"
    '

    # Quick check of both Wi-Fi interfaces
    alias check-wifi='nmcli device status && ip addr show drone_a && ip addr show drone_b'

Then reload your shell:

    source ~/.bashrc

Usage:
    ros-drone-a    (then launch your Tello nodes)
    ros-drone-b    (then launch your Astro nodes)


